This repository is not under a single licence, and every file says which one
applies to it. The SPDX-License-Identifier line at the top of a file is the
authoritative answer for that file; what follows is the map.


0BSD -- everything written for this project
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    LICENSES/0BSD.txt

The build system, the scripts, the rootfs overlay, the userspace sources, the
profiles, the configuration and the documentation are under the BSD Zero Clause
Licence: use it, copy it, change it, ship it, sell it, with or without credit
and without asking. There is no notice to keep and no condition to meet.

This is deliberate. The work is given away. Nobody should have to carry a name
around to be allowed to use it.

The 0BSD grant above covers what this project wrote, and only that. One data
file sitting in those same directories is not this project's work and is not
given away here -- the camera's factory calibration table, measured by others.
THIRD_PARTY.md names it and says what is known about it. Nothing this project
does not own is relicensed by this file.


GPL-2.0 -- the kernel parts, because they cannot be anything else
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt

    patches/**
    drivers/**

These are modifications to, and loadable modules for, the Linux kernel. They
are derivative works of GPL-2.0 code, so GPL-2.0 is not a choice made here --
it is what that code already requires.

Two files under drivers/ are third-party GPL-2.0 code carried in unchanged and
keep their original authors' notices:

    drivers/audio/es7210/  (c) Everest Semiconductor Co., Ltd.

An image built from this repository contains a modified Linux kernel. GPL-2.0
§3 obliges whoever distributes such an image to provide the corresponding
source. sources.lock pins every upstream tree by commit and patches/ carries
every change applied to them; scripts/builder/export-sources.sh packs those
trees, as built, into an archive to ship with the image.


Vendor firmware and libraries -- not here
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No vendor firmware is in this repository: not the touch controller's, not the
Zigbee coordinator's, not Amlogic's trusted applications, video microcode or
Bluetooth firmware, and not the amplifier tuning. This project has no
redistribution grant for any of it. What the repository carries instead is a
list naming those files and where they belong; the board copies them out of
its own storage on first boot, so what ends up in /usr/lib is a copy the owner
made from their own device.

The Amlogic binary libraries are not here either. The image carries their URLs
and checksums, and the board downloads them from Khadas.

One vendor file does go into the image: the W2 Wi-Fi firmware and its RF
table, from Khadas' public driver repository. THIRD_PARTY.md says why.


THIRD_PARTY.md records every piece of third-party material in here, where it
came from and on what terms.
